{"title":"Transitive property","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binary_relation\" title=\"Binary relation\">binary relation</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a074fd0ffda36cd4dbd4b9828f7ae894b62a57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> is said to be <b>transitive</b> or to have the <b>transitive property</b> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a074fd0ffda36cd4dbd4b9828f7ae894b62a57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c517eaa97d8236a2015bffe51d56557932d4d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> together imply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef25d0583285fd7c714b2b6e6c1dc22e24578b79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Transitive_property&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Transitive_property&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partially_ordered_set\" title=\"Partially ordered set\">Partially ordered set</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equivalence_relation\" title=\"Equivalence relation\">Equivalence relation</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018112315\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: fa